</person-group><article-title>Association of levels of HIV-1-infected breast milk cells and risk of mother-to-child transmission</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2004</year><volume>190</volume><fpage>1880</fpage><lpage>1888</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15499546</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/425076</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Semba</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumwenda</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoover</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Taha</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Quinn</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Mtimavalye</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Biggar</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Broadhead</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Miotti</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Sokoll</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Van der</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiphangwi</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human immunodeficiency virus load in breast milk, mastitis, and mother-to-child transmission of human immunodeficiency virus type 1</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>1999</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10353866</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/314854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Semba</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mastitis and transmission of human immunodeficiency virus through breast milk</article-title><source>Ann N Y Acad Sci</source><year>2000</year><volume>918</volume><fpage>15